                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7d494db-6aaf-353f-9fec-0f0a2f629a30",
                        "entry_id": "436f4be0-799a-370f-baee-76217fec5860",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fail in pleasing; displease."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c2351a0-e3b7-4682-837c-a00d8182becc",
                                "sense_id": "f7d494db-6aaf-353f-9fec-0f0a2f629a30",
                                "text": "Oh, i [sic] have one great Fear to misplease Him, and I pray He give me more of that Fear each Day, He my heavenly Father, not the Fear like Olga to the Knout, but to fear I misplease Him my Father, and make me not worthy of His Love."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08c2bf78-61e7-4d8e-b1f4-fcc2f8f620fc",
                                "sense_id": "f7d494db-6aaf-353f-9fec-0f0a2f629a30",
                                "text": "\"[...] Yet let this make me as sorry as it will, still I must on that account above all see how everything looks before God and in itself, how it pleases or mispleases him.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fe02619-81c0-4d18-b7bd-2aa0bf0c16a5",
                                "sense_id": "f7d494db-6aaf-353f-9fec-0f0a2f629a30",
                                "text": "The heart mispleases me that is held coldly, Severely closed amid the years of feeling."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
